WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.901
The capstone transfers the
loop to Harbor Maintenance.

00:00:02.971 --> 00:00:07.281
A sponsor asks for an AI assistant
to route maintenance requests.

00:00:07.351 --> 00:00:13.303
The workflow includes urgent conditions, missing
asset identifiers, duplicate requests, and a

00:00:13.373 --> 00:00:16.103
supervisor who owns priority decisions.

00:00:16.173 --> 00:00:21.208
Keep safety procedures authoritative
and do not automate operational control.

00:00:21.278 --> 00:00:23.795
Your first task is discovery and framing.

00:00:23.865 --> 00:00:29.647
The capstone uses synthetic records and evaluates
how well you preserve evidence and authority

00:00:29.717 --> 00:00:31.466
while building a usable path.

00:00:31.536 --> 00:00:33.776
The sponsor wants automated closure.

00:00:33.846 --> 00:00:39.094
The supervisor needs faster review and
refuses automatic priority changes.

00:00:39.164 --> 00:00:43.281
Historical records include
duplicates and missing asset IDs.

00:00:43.351 --> 00:00:46.018
These differences must appear in your Site Map.

00:00:46.088 --> 00:00:50.867
Pause the video and complete this exercise
before opening the worked response.

00:00:50.937 --> 00:00:53.945
Use the capstone brief and staged evidence pack.

00:00:54.015 --> 00:00:57.833
Submit a Site Map and Frame Card
before opening later results.

00:00:57.903 --> 00:01:03.919
A defensible frame targets supervisor review
time while preserving authorized priority and

00:01:03.989 --> 00:01:05.312
closure decisions.

00:01:05.382 --> 00:01:08.667
Missing identifiers require
a clarification path.

00:01:08.737 --> 00:01:13.964
Duplicate detection supports the reviewer
but does not silently delete a request.

00:01:14.034 --> 00:01:19.154
Any urgent safety text routes to human
assessment under existing procedures.

00:01:19.224 --> 00:01:22.829
Record these as design
boundaries before implementation.

00:01:22.899 --> 00:01:25.630
Who retains maintenance priority authority?

00:01:25.700 --> 00:01:27.236
A. The ticket text B.

00:01:27.306 --> 00:01:29.183
The authorized supervisor C.

00:01:29.253 --> 00:01:30.832
The fastest routing rule.

00:01:30.902 --> 00:01:32.374
The best answer is B.

00:01:32.444 --> 00:01:36.305
The tool assists review without
assuming operating authority.
